{"kind":"request","text":"Claude: a signing command must not pay a cold fold of the whole log each time it runs.\n\nhugh asked on 2026-10-16 why landing in the artroom workroom still takes so long, and approved filing this.\n\nEvery signing command runs the chain preflight and admission against Workspace.Snapshot, a local verified fold: gs state, batch, ratify, supersede, artifact, review-request, promise and land. Examples are cmd/gs/preflight.go:26-30 and 217-225, and internal/app/preflight.go:54 and 95, all at 5876d211. The fold stays local by design, because admission before signing is judged on the local verified log. But each CLI process starts that fold cold, apart from what a checkpoint saves.\n\nMeasured:\n- On a frozen artroom copy at depth 43,744 with no checkpoint, a refused `gs ratify --server` took 54.1 s and 683 MB at head 89c4603b, and 55.5 s on main.\n- `gs state --no-preflight` still spent about 66 s of client CPU, so another site on the submit path also folds locally; BuildActRequest is the likely one.\n- On 2026-10-13, with the live checkpoint at depth 38,186, one local fold took 23 to 28 s.\n\nA lane that publishes an artifact set, requests review, ratifies and lands pays this several times over before any landing cost.\n\nOutcome. First measure the fold cost of each signing command against the real artroom checkout (checkpoint present) and a frozen copy, and find every local fold on the submit path. Then make one signing command cost much less than a cold fold of the log at this depth. The judgement must still rest on a log verified locally: for example, verify only the suffix past a trusted checkpoint, keep the checkpoint current, or reuse a verified local cache across processes. A resident's projection must not take the place of local verification.","body":{"conditions":"1. The report states the measured wall time and peak RSS of gs ratify, gs state, gs artifact and gs review-request on the real artroom checkout (read-only or refused acts only) and on a frozen copy, before and after, naming every local fold on each path. 2. After the change, a signing command at artroom depth performs no full verification of the log when a valid local checkpoint or cache exists at or behind the head; a test counts full scans and goes red if one returns. 3. Admission and preflight still judge against a locally verified log at the head being signed against; no resident projection substitutes for it, and a tampered cache or checkpoint is refused (test pins it). 4. Projections are byte-identical to a cold fold at the same frontier on a frozen copy. 5. go test ./... passes at the head.","target_head":"5876d2118fa3d9d223dfc923744bc0bb9ef1dfc0","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8","to":"a5d35aa7e4799472a208663d7f024917442bd513929f9eccf450628ccf70095d"}}